READ COMMITTED Isolation Level

Objective: To demonstrate how PostgreSQL READ COMMITTED isolation handles concurrent transactions.

Scenario: Two database sessions accessed the same CampusCart product record.

Session A: Started a READ COMMITTED transaction and retrieved the product stock.

Session B: Updated the product stock by one unit and committed the transaction.

Observation: When Session A executed the SELECT statement again, it displayed the updated stock quantity.

Conclusion: PostgreSQL READ COMMITTED provides a fresh snapshot for each SQL statement. Consequently, a transaction can see changes committed by other transactions between its statements.

